            <ArticleTitle>[Diagnostic image (284). A man with Horner's syndrome, ipsilateral headache and dysphasia].</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>1673</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>A 56-year-old man presented with sudden dysphasia and dyspraxia. He had noticed a small left pupil and had suffered from left-sided headache two weeks previously. MRI revealed dissection of the left inner carotid artery.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
